169301,"It was narrated to me by Yahya, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Aslam, the freed slave of Umar ibn al-Khattab, that Umar ibn al-Khattab ruled that a molar tooth incurs a camel, and a collarbone incurs a camel, and a rib incurs a camel."
169302,"From Yahya ibn Sa'id, that Umar ibn al-Khattab was eating bread with ghee. He invited a man from the desert, and he began to eat, following the morsel with the edge of the dish. Umar said: It is as if you are destitute. He said: By Allah, I have not eaten ghee, nor have I seen anyone eat with it, for such and such a time. Umar said: I will not eat ghee until people are well-provided for from the beginning of their sustenance."
169401,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Wahb ibn Kaysan that Jabir ibn Abdullah said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, sent a delegation to the coast. Abu Ubayda ibn al- Jarrah was in command of them. There were 300 people and I was among them. We went out until we had gone part of the way and our provisions were finished. Abu Ubayda ordered that the provisions of the army be gathered up and they amounted to two containers of dates. He used to give us a little provision from it each day until it was finished, and we used to have only a single date each. I said, 'What use is one date?' He said, 'We will certainly feel its loss when they are finished.' "" Jabir continued, ""Then we reached the sea and there was a fish like a small mountain. The army ate from it for eighteen nights. Then Abu Ubayda ordered two ribs from it to be set up. Then he commanded that a camel be ridden underneath them and it did not touch them"
169402,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Wahb ibn Kaysan that Jabir ibn Abdullah said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, sent a delegation to the coast. Abu Ubayda ibn al- Jarrah was in command of them. There were 300 people and I was among them. We went out until we had gone part of the way and our provisions were finished. Abu Ubayda ordered that the provisions of the army be gathered up and they amounted to two containers of dates. He used to give us a little provision from it each day until it was finished, and we used to have only a single date each. I said, 'What use is one date?' He said, 'We will certainly feel its loss when they are finished.' "" Jabir continued, ""Then we reached the sea and there was a fish like a small mountain. The army ate from it for eighteen nights. Then Abu Ubayda ordered two ribs from it to be set up. Then he commanded that a camel be ridden underneath them and it did not touch them"
169501,Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Amr ibn Sad ibn Muadh from his grandmother that the Messenger of Allah
169502,Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Amr ibn Sad ibn Muadh from his grandmother that the Messenger of Allah
169601,"Yahya related to me from Malik that Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr said, ""I heard my father say, 'The people used to be ordered to hasten to the meal when the food was served and prayer had been called.'"""
169602,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn that Abu Ghatafan ibn Tarif al-Murri informed him that Marwan ibn al-Hakam sent him to Abdullah ibn Abbas to ask him what there was for the molar. Abdullah ibn Abbas said, ""There are five camels for it."" He said, ""Marwan sent me back again to Abdullah ibn Abbas.'' He said, ""Do you make front teeth like molars?"" Abdullah ibn Abbas said, ""It is enough that you take the fingers as the example for that, their blood-moneys being all the same."""""""
169701,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Isa ibn Maryam used to say
169702,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Isa ibn Maryam used to say
169801,Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard that the Messenger of Allah
169802,Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard that the Messenger of Allah
169901,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn al-Khattab was eating bread with ghee. He summoned one of the desert people and he began to eat and follow the grease in the dish with a morsel of bread. Umar said, ""It is as if you were poor."" He said, ""By Allah. I have not eaten ghee nor have I seen food with it since such- and-such a time."" Umar declared, ""I shall not eat clarified butter until people are given life again like they were first given life,"" (i.e. on the Day of Rising)"
169902,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn al-Khattab was eating bread with ghee. He summoned one of the desert people and he began to eat and follow the grease in the dish with a morsel of bread. Umar said, ""It is as if you were poor."" He said, ""By Allah. I have not eaten ghee nor have I seen food with it since such- and-such a time."" Umar declared, ""I shall not eat clarified butter until people are given life again like they were first given life,"" (i.e. on the Day of Rising)"
170001,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha that Anas ibn Malik said, ""We would pray asr and anyone who then went to the Bani Amr ibn Awf would find them praying asr"
170002,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha that Anas ibn Malik said, ""We would pray asr and anyone who then went to the Bani Amr ibn Awf would find them praying asr"
170101,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""On one occasion when the people were praying subhat Quba a man came to them and said, 'A piece of Qur'an was sent down to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, last night, and he was ordered to face the Kaba, so face it.' They had been facing ash-Sham, so they turned round and faced the Kaba"
170102,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""On one occasion when the people were praying subhat Quba a man came to them and said, 'A piece of Qur'an was sent down to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, last night, and he was ordered to face the Kaba, so face it.' They had been facing ash-Sham, so they turned round and faced the Kaba"
170201,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhala that Humayd ibn Malik ibn Khu'haym said, ""I was sitting with Abu Hurayra on his land at al-Aqiq. Some people rode out from Madina to call upon Abu Hurayra. He told me to go to his mother, sending his greetings and asking her to prepare some food."" Humayd continued, ""She set down three loaves on a plate and some oil and salt. Then she put it on my head and I carried it to them. When I set it before them, Abu Hurayra said, 'Allah is greater' and added, 'Praise be to Allah who has filled us with bread after our food had previously been only water and dates,' as the people did not touch any of the food. When they left, he said, 'O son of my brother, be good to your sheep and wipe the mucus from them and clean their pen. Pray in their quarter for they are among the animals of the Garden. By He in Whose Hand my self is, a time is about to come upon people when a small group of sheep will be more beloved to their owner than the house of Marwan"
170202,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhala that Humayd ibn Malik ibn Khu'haym said, ""I was sitting with Abu Hurayra on his land at al-Aqiq. Some people rode out from Madina to call upon Abu Hurayra. He told me to go to his mother, sending his greetings and asking her to prepare some food."" Humayd continued, ""She set down three loaves on a plate and some oil and salt. Then she put it on my head and I carried it to them. When I set it before them, Abu Hurayra said, 'Allah is greater' and added, 'Praise be to Allah who has filled us with bread after our food had previously been only water and dates,' as the people did not touch any of the food. When they left, he said, 'O son of my brother, be good to your sheep and wipe the mucus from them and clean their pen. Pray in their quarter for they are among the animals of the Garden. By He in Whose Hand my self is, a time is about to come upon people when a small group of sheep will be more beloved to their owner than the house of Marwan"
170301,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Nuaym that Wahb ibn Kaysan said, ""I saw Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr praying while he held his robe with his teeth because of the intensity of his fear of Allah."""
170302,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Nuaym that Wahb ibn Kaysan said, ""Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr said to me, 'O nephew! Do not eat except what is lawful, and do not drink except what is lawful.'"""
170401,Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said that he had heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say that a man came to Abdullah ibn Abbas and said to him
170402,Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said that he had heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say that a man came to Abdullah ibn Abbas and said to him
170501,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father never brought food or drink
170502,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father never brought food or drink
170601,"Malik narrated to me from Yahya ibn Sa'id from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb that a man from Banu Mudlij, named Qatadah, struck his son with a sword, hitting his leg. The wound was cauterized and he died. Surakah ibn Ju'shum came to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and informed him. 'Umar said to him: ""Count out 120 camels at the water of Qudayd until I come to you."" When 'Umar ibn al-Khattab arrived, he took from those camels 30 hiqqah (three-year-old she-camels), 30 jadh'ah (four-year-old she-camels), and 40 khulafah (pregnant she-camels). Then he said, ""Where is the brother of the slain?"" He said, ""Here I am."" He said, ""Take them, for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'There is nothing for the killer.'"""""""
170602,"From Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf that he said: 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah saw Sahl ibn Hunayf bathing and said: ""I have not seen the like of today, not even the skin of a maiden."" Sahl fell ill. He was brought to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and it was said: ""O Messenger of Allah, do you have anything for Sahl ibn Hunayf? By Allah, he cannot raise his head."" He said: ""Do you suspect anyone for him?"" They said: ""We suspect 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called 'Amir, was angry with him, and said: ""Why does one of you kill his brother? Why did you not bless him? Perform wudu for him."" 'Amir washed his face, hands, elbows, knees, feet, and the inside of his lower garment in a vessel, then it was poured over him. Sahl went with the people, nothing ailing him. Muwatta Imam Malik, Hadith 1706."
170701,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said, ""The nobility of the mumin is his taqwa. His deen is his noble descent. His manliness is his good character. Boldness and cowardice are but instincts which Allah places wherever He wills. The coward shrinks from defending even his father and mother, and the bold one fights for the sake of the combat not for the spoils. Being slain is but one way of meeting death, and the martyr is the one who gives himself, expectant of reward from Allah"
170702,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Umar ibn al-Khattab said, ""The nobility of the mumin is his taqwa. His deen is his noble descent. His manliness is his good character. Boldness and cowardice are but instincts which Allah places wherever He wills. The coward shrinks from defending even his father and mother, and the bold one fights for the sake of the combat not for the spoils. Being slain is but one way of meeting death, and the martyr is the one who gives himself, expectant of reward from Allah"
170801,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah
170802,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah
170901,"Yahya related to me from Malik that Sadaqa ibn Yasar said, ""I heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say, 'There is no harm in eating food cooked by the People of the Book, as long as one knows that it does not contain anything unlawful.'"""
170902,"When a servant falls ill, Allah the Exalted sends two angels to him and says: ""Look at what he says to his visitors."" If, when they come to him, he praises Allah and extols Him, they raise that to Allah Almighty—and He knows best—and He says: ""It is incumbent upon Me that if I take his soul, I will admit him to Paradise, and if I cure him, I will replace his flesh with better flesh and his blood with better blood, and I will expiate his sins."""""""
171001,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from Abbad ibn Tamim that Abu Bashir al-Ansari told him that he was with the Messenger of Allah
171002,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr from Abbad ibn Tamim that Abu Bashir al-Ansari told him that he was with the Messenger of Allah
171101,Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf heard his father say
171102,Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abi Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf heard his father say
171201,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Umar ibn Husayn, the mawla of A'isha bint Qudama, that Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan imposed retaliation against a man who killed a mawla with a stick and so the mawla's patron killed the man with a stick. Malik said, ""The generally agreed on way of doing things in our community about which there is no dispute is that when a man strikes another man with a stick or hits him with a rock or intentionally strikes him causing his death, that is an intentional injury and there is retaliation for it."" Malik said, ""Intentional murder with us is that a man intentionally goes to a man and strikes him until his life goes. Part of intentional injury also is that a man strikes a man in a quarrel between them. He leaves him while he is alive, and he bleeds to death and so dies. There is retaliation for that."" Malik said, ""What is done in our community is that a group of free men are killed for the intentional murder of one free man, and a group of women for one woman, and a group of slaves for one slave."""""""
171202,"Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab that Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf said, ""I saw a man who had prayed in the sun until his shadow disappeared, and I do not know anyone who did more of that than him among us."""
171301,"Yahya narrated to me from Malik that it reached him that Marwan ibn al-Hakam wrote to Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan mentioning that a drunkard who had killed a man was brought to him. Mu'awiyah wrote back: ""Kill him for it."" Yahya said: Malik said: The best interpretation I have heard for this verse — Allah's words: {The free for the free, the slave for the slave, and the female for the female} (2:178) — is that these are the males, {and the female for the female} means qisas (retaliation) is between females as it is between males. A free woman is killed for a free woman as a free man is killed for a free man; a slave woman is killed for a slave woman as a slave is killed for a slave. Qisas is between women as it is between men, and qisas is also between men and women. Allah says in His Book: {And We ordained for them therein: life for life, eye for eye, nose for nose, ear for ear, tooth for tooth, and wounds equal for equal} (5:45). Allah mentions life for life, so the life of a free woman is for the life of a free man, and her wound for his wound. Malik said concerning a man who holds a man for another man who strikes him and he dies on the spot: if he held him knowing he intended to kill him, both are killed for it. If he held him thinking he only intended to strike as people strike, not intending to kill, the killer is killed and the holder is severely punished and imprisoned for a year, because he held him, but there is no killing on him. Malik said concerning a man who kills a man intentionally or gouges his eye intentionally: the killer is killed or the gouger's eye is gouged."
171302,"Yahya related to me from Malik that Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki said, ""A man came to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said, 'Messenger of Allah, I have committed a sin which requires that a legal punishment be inflicted on me, so inflict it on me.' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, did not ask him what he had done. Then the time for the prayer came, and the man prayed with the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. When the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, had finished the prayer, the man stood up again and said, 'Messenger of Allah, I have committed a sin, so inflict on me the legal punishment for it.' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'Have you not prayed with us?' He said, 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'Allah has forgiven you your sin,' or he said, 'your legal punishment.'"""
171401,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Urwa ibn az-Zubayr told him that the Messenger of Allah
171402,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Urwa ibn az-Zubayr told him that the Messenger of Allah
171501,Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that the Messenger of Allah
171502,Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar that the Messenger of Allah
171601,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yazid ibn Khusayfa that Urwa ibn az-Zubayr said that he heard A'isha
171602,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yazid ibn Khusayfa that Urwa ibn az-Zubayr said that he heard A'isha
171701,Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sasaca said that he heard Abu'l-Hubab Said ibn Yasar say that he had heard Abu Hurayra say
171702,Yahya related to me from Malik that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sasaca said that he heard Abu'l-Hubab Said ibn Yasar say that he had heard Abu Hurayra say
171801,"Yahya narrated to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Bushayr ibn Yasar that he informed him that 'Abdullah ibn Sahl al-Ansari and Muhayyisah ibn Mas'ud went to Khaybar. They separated for their needs. 'Abdullah ibn Sahl was killed. Muhayyisah came, and he, his brother Huwayyisah, and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl came to the Prophet (ﷺ). 'Abd al-Rahman began to speak because of his closeness to his brother. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Let the elder speak, let the elder speak."" So Huwayyisah and Muhayyisah spoke and mentioned the matter of 'Abdullah ibn Sahl. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Will you swear fifty oaths and thereby claim the blood of your companion or your killer?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we did not witness nor were we present."" He said: ""Then the Jews will exonerate themselves with fifty oaths."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, how can we accept the oaths of a disbelieving people?"" Yahya ibn Sa'id said: Bushayr ibn Yasar claimed that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) paid the blood money from his own wealth. Malik said: The agreed ruling with us, which I heard from those I trust, regarding qasama (oaths in homicide), and upon which the Imams agreed in past and present, is that the claimants begin the oaths in qasama. Qasama is only obligatory in one of two cases: either the slain says, ""My blood is with so-and-so,"" or the heirs of the blood bring a luth (circumstantial evidence) that is not conclusive against the accused. This obligates qasama for the claimants against the accused. Qasama is not obligatory with us except by one of these two ways. Malik said: This is the undisputed Sunnah with us, upon which people have always acted: the ones who begin qasama are the heirs of the blood, those who claim intentional or unintentional killing. Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began with the Harithis in the killing of their companion at Khaybar. Malik said: If the claimants swear, they are entitled to the blood of their companion and kill the one they swore against. No more than one is killed in qasama; two are not killed. Fifty men from the heirs of the blood swear fifty oaths. If their number is less or some refuse, the oaths are repeated upon them, unless one of the heirs of the slain who have the right to pardon refuses. If one of them refuses, there is no way to the blood. Yahya said: Malik said: The oaths are repeated upon those remaining only if the one who refused is not entitled to pardon. If one of the heirs of the blood who are entitled to pardon refuses, even if only one, the oaths are not repeated upon the remaining heirs. But in that case, the oaths are repeated upon the accused: fifty of them swear fifty oaths. If they are not fifty, the oaths are repeated upon those who swore. If only the accused is found, he swears fifty oaths and is exonerated. Yahya said: Malik said: The difference between qasama in blood and oaths in property rights is that when a man lends to another, he secures his right; but when a man intends to kill another, he does not kill him in a gathering, he seeks seclusion. If qasama were only where evidence is established, and conducted like property rights, blood would be lost and people would be emboldened when they know the judgment. But qasama was given to the heirs of the slain to begin, so that people may refrain from blood and the killer may fear being seized by the word of the slain. Yahya said: Malik said concerning a people who have an enemy suspected of the blood: the heirs of the slain repeat the oaths upon them, and they are a group with numbers. Each man swears fifty oaths for himself; the oaths are not divided proportionally to their number, nor are they exonerated until each swears fifty oaths for himself. Malik said: This is the best I have heard on this. Qasama belongs to the 'asaba (paternal relatives) of the slain; they are the heirs of the blood who swear and by whose qasama killing occurs."
