178701,"Yahya related to me from Malik that Umar ibn al-Khattab asked a man what his name was. He said, ""Jamra (live coal)."" ""The son of who?"" He said, ""Ibn Shihab (meteor, flame)."" ""From whom?"" He said, ""From al-Huraqa (burning)."" ""Where do you live?"" He said, ""At Harrat an-Nar (lava field of the fire)."" ""At which one of them?"" He said, ""At Dhati Ladha (one with flames)."" Umar said, ""Go and look at your family - they have been burned."" Yahya added, ""It was as Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said - the man went back and found that his family had indeed been burned in a fire that had swept through their dwelling."""
178702,"Yahya related to me from Malik that Umar ibn al-Khattab asked a man what his name was. He said, ""Jamra (live coal)."" ""The son of who?"" He said, ""Ibn Shihab (meteor, flame)."" ""From whom?"" He said, ""From al-Huraqa (burning)."" ""Where do you live?"" He said, ""At Harrat an-Nar (lava field of the fire)."" ""At which one of them?"" He said, ""At Dhati Ladha (one with flames)."" Umar said, ""Go and look at your family - they have been burned."" Yahya added, ""It was as Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said - his family had indeed been burned, just as their names had foretold."""
178801,"Malik related to me from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, used to visit Umm Haram bint Milhan, and she used to feed him. Umm Haram was the wife of Ubada ibn as-Samit. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, visited her and she fed him. Then she sat down and began looking through his head for lice, and the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, went to sleep. Then he woke up laughing. She said, 'What makes you laugh, Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Some people of my community were shown to me, fighting in the way of Allah, sailing on this sea, kings on couches, or like kings on couches.' (Ishaq is not sure which is correct.) She said, 'Messenger of Allah, make du'a to Allah that He make me one of them.' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, made du'a for her. Then he went to sleep again, then he woke up laughing. She said, 'What makes you laugh, Messenger of Allah?' He said the same as he had said the first time. She said, 'Messenger of Allah, make du'a to Allah that He make me one of them.' He said, 'You are among the first' (or, 'You are one of the first ones'). Umm Haram bint Milhan sailed on the sea in the time of Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan and fell down"
178802,"Malik related to me from Humayd at-Tawil that Anas ibn Malik said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'Make things easy and do not make them difficult, make people calm and cheerful and do not drive them away.'"""
178901,Malik related to me that he heard that the Messenger of Allah
178902,"From Abu al-Sa'ib, mawla of Hisham ibn Zuhrah, that he said: I entered upon Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and found him praying. I sat waiting until he finished. I heard a rustling under a bed in his house — a snake. I stood to kill it. Abu Sa'id gestured to me to sit. When he finished, he gestured to a room in the house and said: ""Do you see this house?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""There was a young man in it, recently married. He went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to the Trench. While he was there, the young man asked permission: 'O Messenger of Allah, permit me to visit my family.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) permitted him and said: 'Take your weapon, for I fear Banu Qurayzah for you.' The young man went to his family and found his wife standing between the two doors. He lunged at her with his spear to stab her, but a ghayrah (protective jealousy) overtook her. She said: 'Do not hasten until you enter and see what is in your house.' He entered and found a snake coiled on his bed. He thrust his spear into it, then came out with it and planted it in the courtyard. The snake thrashed on the spearhead, and the young man fell dead. It was not known which died first, the young man or the snake. This was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: 'In Medina there are jinn who have become Muslim. If you see any of them, give them three days' notice. If they appear after that, kill them, for they are devils.'"" Muwatta Imam Malik, Hadith 1789."
179001,Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Ibn Muhayyisa al-Ansari
179002,Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Ibn Muhayyisa al-Ansari
179101,"Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of fruit until its good condition was evident."""
179102,"Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""A man asked the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, 'Which Islam is the best?' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'That you feed people and give the greeting of peace to people you know and people you do not know.'"""
