180501,"It was narrated to me from Malik, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a disbelieving guest was hosted by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered a sheep to be milked for him, and he drank its milk. Then another was milked, and he drank its milk. Then another was milked, and he drank its milk, until he drank the milk of seven sheep. The next morning, he became Muslim. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered a sheep to be milked for him, and he drank its milk. Then he ordered another to be milked, but he did not finish it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The believer drinks in one intestine"
180502,"It was narrated from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever says to his brother"
180601,Malik related to me from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
180602,Malik related to me from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
180701,"Malik related to me that he heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw a female slave belonging to Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab. She was dressed like free (non-slave) women. He went to his daughter Hafsa and said, ""Didn't I see your brother's slave-girl dressed like a free (non-slave) woman walking among the people and causing trouble?"" Umar disapproved of that"
180702,"Malik related to me that he heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw a female slave belonging to Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab. She was dressed like free (non-slave) women. He went to his daughter Hafsa and said, ""Didn't I see your brother's slave-girl dressed like a free (non-slave) woman walking among the people and causing trouble?"" Umar disapproved of that"
180801,"Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling the fruit until it was clear that it was ripe."""
180802,"Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, forbade selling fruits until they were ripe."""
180901,"Malik related to me from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir that Umayma bint Ruqayqa said, ""I came to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, with some other women to give him our allegiance. We said, 'We give you our allegiance that we will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, will not commit fornication, will not kill our children, will not produce slander, and will not disobey you in what is right.' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'As for what you are able to do and are capable of.' We said, 'Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than we are to ourselves. Come, let us give you our allegiance, Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'I do not shake hands with women. My word to a hundred women is like my word to one woman.'"""
180902,"Malik related to me from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir that Umayma bint Ruqayqa said, ""I came to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, with some women to swear allegiance to him. We said, 'We give you our allegiance that we will not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill our children, nor bring lies which we have devised, nor disobey you in what is right.' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'As much as you are able to do.'"" She said, ""We said, 'Allah is more merciful to us than ourselves. Come, let us give you our hand, Messenger of Allah!' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'I do not shake hands with women. What I say to a hundred women is like what I say to one woman.'"""
181001,Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abdullah ibn Umar wrote to Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan
