181601,"Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abu Salih as- Samman informed him that Abu Hurayra said, ""Truly a man utters words to which he attaches no importance, and by them he falls into the fire of Jahannam, and truly a man utters words to which he attaches no importance, and by them Allah raises him into the Garden"
181602,"Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Dinar that Abu Salih as- Samman informed him that Abu Hurayra said, ""Truly a man utters words to which he attaches no importance, and by them he falls into the fire of Jahannam, and truly a man utters words to which he attaches no importance, and by them Allah raises him into the Garden"
181701,"Malik related to me from Zayd ibn Aslam that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""None of you should sell what he does not have."""
181702,"Malik related to me from Zayd ibn Aslam that Abdullah ibn Umar said, ""A man came to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and asked him, 'What things are forbidden while in ihram?' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'Do not wear a shirt, or a turban, or trousers, or a burnous, or shoes, unless you cannot find sandals, in which case wear shoes and cut them so that they are below the ankles. Do not wear any garment which has been touched by saffron or wars (a plant used for dying).'"""
181801,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Sumayy, the mawla of Abu Bakr from Abu Salih as-Samman from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, ""A man was walking on a road when he became very thirsty. He found a well and went into it and drank and came out. There was a dog panting and eating earth out of thirst. The man said, 'This dog has become as thirsty as I was.' He went down into the well and filled his shoe and then held it in his mouth until he climbed out and gave the dog water to drink. Allah thanked him for it and forgave him."" They said, ""Messenger of Allah, do we have a reward for taking care of beasts?"" He said, ""There is a reward for every one with a moist liver."""""""
181802,Malik related to me that he heard that Isa ibn Maryam used to say
181901,"Malik narrated to me from Wahb ibn Kaysan from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah that he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent an expedition toward the coast and appointed Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah over them. They were three hundred. I was among them. We set out until, at some point on the way, our provisions ran out. Abu 'Ubaydah ordered the provisions of that army to be collected. All of it was gathered, and it amounted to two bags of dates. He rationed us a little each day until it was finished. We got nothing but one date each. I said: ""What good is one date?"" He said: ""We felt its loss when it was gone."" Then we reached the sea. There was a fish like a small mountain. That army ate from it for eighteen nights. Then Abu 'Ubaydah ordered two of its ribs to be set up. He ordered a camel to be saddled, and it passed under them without touching them."
181902,"It was narrated from Safwan ibn Sulaym, that a man said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): \Should I lie to my wife"
182001,Malik related to me from al-Walid ibn Abdullah ibn Sayyad that al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab al-Makhzumi informed him that a man asked the Messenger of Allah
182002,Malik related to me from al-Walid ibn Abdullah ibn Sayyad that al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab al-Makhzumi informed him that a man asked the Messenger of Allah
